 "judge_section_notes": "The final text is a Northwind-favourable package that was never signed by Halcyon: S2 sets an 8% ceiling with no mandatory sales stop, so the Hearth 10 (6.2%) is spared while the Ember 8 is not directly affected, and per-model results go to buyers and regulators but not the public. S5 makes recall mandatory above 8 per 100,000, which would hit Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, while S4's 36-month suppression deadline favours Halcyon on cost. S3 allows 24 months for new units and 6 years for retrofits with an open 'where technically feasible' escape, which benefits Northwind given its 38% shut-off coverage.",
